; --- Codex stack: earned fate / destiny against locked one (ADR 0065) --------
;
; Same three-state discipline as the institution stack above, for the same reason:
; "Earned, never chosen" is only legible if a thing the hero OWNS never looks
; like a thing they do not. So the three entries are distinct surfaces, not one
; card in three greys — an earned card sits on the brighter `card` ink with the
; warm gold edge a filled seat gets, a locked card recedes into the list-panel
; ink with a hairline ash border, and a destiny card (the loudest thing in the
; codex) takes the gold edge at a heavier weight than either.

[sub_resource type="StyleBoxFlat" id="earned_card"]
bg_color = Color(0.114, 0.114, 0.137, 1)
border_width_left = 1
border_width_top = 1
border_width_right = 1
border_width_bottom = 1
border_color = Color(0.478, 0.408, 0.239, 1)
corner_radius_top_left = 3
corner_radius_top_right = 3
corner_radius_bottom_right = 3
corner_radius_bottom_left = 3
content_margin_left = 10.0
content_margin_top = 8.0
content_margin_right = 10.0
content_margin_bottom = 8.0

